data: {"type": "assistant_msg", "ts": "2026-08-06T12:21:10.499601+00:00", "content": "Based on the live telemetry gathered for **ce_branch24**, here is the investigation summary:\n\n## Device Health (ce_branch24) \u2014 **Healthy**\n- **Hardware**: Fan 3000 RPM, power draw 72.5 W, PSU voltage 11.88 V, chassis temp 29 \u00b0C \u2014 all within normal ranges.\n- **Transceiver**: RX \u20135.99 dBm, temp 37 \u00b0C, TX bias 28.2 mA \u2014 solid optical link.\n- **System**: CPU 0.16 %, memory 0.19 % \u2014 negligible load.\n\n## SD-WAN Tunnel (wg0) \u2014 **Operational, Good Quality**\n- Path active, latency 70.85 ms, jitter 6.83 ms, loss 0.079 %, 4 rekeys \u2014 well within typical SLA bounds.\n\n## Interface Counters & Discards \u2014 **Attention on eth0**\n| Interface | Role / VRF | In (octets) | Out (octets) | In Discards | Queue Drops |\n|-----------|------------|-------------|--------------|-------------|-------------|\n| **eth0** (ifIndex 2) | LAN / primary uplink | 9.9 M | 3.8 M | **1,877** | **90** |\n| eth1 (ifIndex 515) | LAN secondary | 105 k | 80 k | 0 | 2 |\n| eth2/eth3/eth4 | Low-usage ports | < 2 k each | < 2 k each | 0 | 0 |\n| **wg0** | SD-WAN overlay | 940 k | 961 k | 0 | \u2014 |\n| **vrf_CORP** | Corporate VRF | 56 k | 0 | 0 | \u2014 |\n| **vrf_VOICE** | Voice VRF | 54 k | 0 | 0 | \u2014 |\n\n**Key finding**: eth0 shows **1,877 input discards** and **90 queue drops** \u2014 the only interface with non-zero discards/drops. This suggests intermittent burst congestion or a speed/duplex mismatch on the primary LAN uplink.\n\n## Topology Blast-Radius (2 hops)\n- **Upstream**: pe12 (PE router) \u2014 BGP established (2 peers), MPLS LDP up, OSPF full, 113 LSPs \u2014 **healthy core**.\n- **Downstream neighbors**: h_branch24_corp, h_branch24_voice (no metrics exposed).\n- **Sibling branches**: ce_branch12 (similar hardware, slightly higher SD-WAN loss 2.6 %), p23/p24 (core P routers, normal).\n\n## Logs & Flows\n- **No syslog/events** returned in the investigation window.\n- **No flow records** returned.\n\n## Runbooks / Past Incidents\n- KB search backend temporarily unavailable; no automated runbook or incident matches retrieved.\n\n---\n\n## Recommendation\n1. **Investigate eth0 discards/drops**: check for CRC errors, speed/duplex negotiation, or cable/port faults on the primary LAN uplink. A `show interface eth0` and `show interface counters errors` on the device would be the next step.\n2. **Monitor SD-WAN metrics** \u2014 currently healthy, but keep an eye on loss/jitter if eth0 issues persist (traffic traverses wg0).\n3. **No immediate action** on pe12, sibling branches, or core \u2014 all telemetry is clean.\n\nThe device itself is stable; the only anomaly is the eth0 input discards/queue drops."}

